<section class="hero wrap">
<div class="eyebrow">Editorial Accountability · Public Policy</div>
<h1>CORRECTIONS AND RIGHT OF REPLY.</h1>
<p class="lead">Matrix Reprogrammed investigates public records, institutions, relationships and contested claims. Accuracy requires a clear route to challenge, correct, clarify or supplement what has been published.</p>
<div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=correction">Request a Correction</a><a class="btn alt" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=right-of-reply">Submit a Right of Reply</a><a class="btn alt" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=evidence">Submit Supporting Evidence</a></div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap split">
<div>
<div class="eyebrow">What We Will Review</div>
<h2>A SPECIFIC CLAIM, A SPECIFIC RECORD, A SPECIFIC REMEDY.</h2>
<p>A useful correction request identifies the exact page, statement, date, profile, chart or relationship being challenged. It should explain what is wrong, provide the strongest available evidence and state the correction or clarification requested.</p>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card redline"><span class="label">Correction</span><h3>Factually inaccurate</h3><p>A name, date, role, figure, quotation, ownership statement, legal status, relationship or source description is demonstrably wrong.</p></article>
<article class="card redline"><span class="label">Clarification</span><h3>Technically true but misleading</h3><p>A statement omits material context, uses an imprecise label or could reasonably create a false impression.</p></article>
<article class="card redline"><span class="label">Right of reply</span><h3>Affected person or organisation</h3><p>A living subject, organisation or authorised representative may submit a response, denial, explanation or supporting record for editorial review.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
<aside class="card redline">
<div class="pill">Required information</div>
<h2>Include enough detail to verify.</h2>
<ul>
<li>The exact page URL and disputed statement.</li>
<li>Your name, role and authority to speak, when relevant.</li>
<li>Primary documents, official records or reliable source links.</li>
<li>The correction, clarification or reply requested.</li>
<li>Any deadline and the reason it matters.</li>
</ul>
<p class="warning">Anonymous assertions are reviewed, but they do not automatically outweigh documented public records.</p>
</aside>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
<div class="eyebrow">Editorial Process</div>
<h2>HOW A REQUEST IS HANDLED.</h2>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><span class="label">1 · Log</span><h3>Request recorded</h3><p>The submission is routed into the corrections and right-of-reply review lane with the page, claim, evidence and contact details supplied.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="label">2 · Verify</span><h3>Evidence compared</h3><p>The published claim is checked against its original sources, stronger records, credible counter-evidence and any response from the affected party.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="label">3 · Decide</span><h3>Outcome classified</h3><p>The result may be correction, clarification, contextual addition, source replacement, right-of-reply publication, no change or temporary removal pending review.</p></article>
<article class="card"><span class="label">4 · Record</span><h3>Material change preserved</h3><p>Substantive corrections should identify what changed and why. Evidence classifications, confidence and unresolved questions are updated where necessary.</p></article>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap split">
<div class="card redline">
<div class="eyebrow">Evidence Boundaries</div>
<h2>WHAT A CORRECTION DOES NOT MEAN.</h2>
<p>Correcting one statement does not validate every alternative claim. Publishing a reply does not mean Matrix Reprogrammed accepts it as fact. Declining a requested change does not prove wrongdoing or bad faith.</p>
<p>Documented fact, official allegation, analytical inference, disputed claim and deep speculation remain separate evidence classes.</p>
</div>
<div class="card">
<div class="eyebrow">Safety and Privacy</div>
<h2>PROTECT VICTIMS, MINORS AND SOURCES.</h2>
<p>Do not submit illegal material, passwords, stolen credentials, private intimate content, graphic exploitation material or identifying information that could endanger a victim, minor or protected source.</p>
<p>Use the PGP route on <a href="contact-the-machine.html#secure-pgp">Contact the Machine</a> for sensitive but lawful documentary material. Encryption protects content, not complete anonymity.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section wrap">
<div class="eyebrow">Submission Routes</div>
<h2>OPEN THE CORRECT CHANNEL.</h2>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card redline"><h3>Correction request</h3><p>Challenge a factual statement or request a documented clarification.</p><a class="btn" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=correction">Open correction form</a></article>
<article class="card redline"><h3>Right of reply</h3><p>Submit an attributable response as a subject or authorised representative.</p><a class="btn" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=right-of-reply">Open reply form</a></article>
<article class="card redline"><h3>Evidence submission</h3><p>Provide a filing, judgment, register extract, annual report, archive or other verifiable record.</p><a class="btn" href="contact-the-machine.html?topic=evidence">Open evidence form</a></article>
</div>
</section>
